  "notes": "Cause code X ('Other') governs category despite narrative's root-cause language pointing toward a personnel/conservative-decision-making theme; theme field captures this nuance. UPS HVAC X-01's cross-connection to CCW Train 1-B kept it functional for the whole event per Section III.A, but this describes ongoing condenser cooling capability rather than a distinct 'backup system' being invoked during a stated inoperability window for X-01 itself (X-01 itself was declared inoperable due to non-realignment) - not modeled as BACKED_UP_BY given ambiguity/overlap with the failure chain itself. No ADS/HPCI/RCIC-type systems present in this narrative. Previous similar event LER 445/03-004-00 modeled as stub per rule 9; root cause of that prior event was explicitly stated as unrelated to CCW alignment, included in notes rather than as a queryable claim since it's descriptive text, not a graph relation the schema supports well beyond SIMILAR_TO."
